Use slightly warm cinematic color grading with restrained saturation.

--------------------------------------------------
CAMERA & FRAMING
--------------------------------------------------

Vertical cinematic portrait.

Use a medium-wide seated composition.

Show approximately:
- complete head
- neck
- shoulders
- chest
- torso
- arms
- waist
- upper legs / part of the seated lower body

The framing should feel slightly distant rather than close.

The person must NOT fill the entire image.

Leave generous environmental space around the subject so the library, windows, furniture, and atmosphere remain clearly visible.

The person should occupy approximately 45–60% of the frame height.

Use some negative space around the head and body.

Camera approximately at seated chest level or slightly below eye level.

Professional full-frame camera look.

Approximately 50–85mm lens.

Natural perspective.
No wide-angle face distortion.

